532
00:58:29.730 --> 00:58:35.410
<v Speaker 2>So what happens through this exercise is that we get to the true concept of Tawheed.

533
00:58:37.490 --> 00:58:44.210
<v Speaker 2>The concept of Tawheed is not that Allah is the ultimate deity in a hierarchy of deity.

534
00:58:46.050 --> 00:58:50.370
<v Speaker 2>The concept of Tawheed is not that Allah is the ultimate God in a hierarchy of gods.

535
00:58:50.370 --> 00:58:50.610
<v Speaker 2>No.

536
00:58:51.170 --> 00:58:54.690
<v Speaker 2>The concept of Tawheed is that there is no other deity.

537
00:58:55.130 --> 00:59:01.810
<v Speaker 2>There is a complete elimination of all other deities.

538
00:59:03.010 --> 00:59:05.650
<v Speaker 2>Except the one and only deity which is Allah.

539
00:59:06.450 --> 00:59:13.570
<v Speaker 2>It is the transference of ilahiya from its generic form to one specific being that has no form.

540
00:59:15.090 --> 00:59:18.410
<v Speaker 2>That is the challenge and the goal of La ilaha illallah.

541
00:59:21.810 --> 00:59:22.130
<v Speaker 2>Right?

542
00:59:22.450 --> 00:59:23.490
<v Speaker 2>And how do we do this?

543
00:59:23.490 --> 00:59:26.770
<v Speaker 2>Slowly, gradually, one by one, one idol at a time.

544
00:59:28.290 --> 00:59:33.330
<v Speaker 2>Just with the sword of La ilaha illallah we keep striking at the idol.

545
00:59:33.410 --> 00:59:35.970
<v Speaker 2>We're not going to break every idol in one strike.

546
00:59:36.410 --> 00:59:39.490
<v Speaker 2>It might take a lot of strikes to quit a habit.

547
00:59:41.250 --> 00:59:42.930
<v Speaker 2>It might take a lot of effort

548
00:59:43.330 --> 00:59:45.650
<v Speaker 2>to reject the desire.

549
00:59:45.970 --> 00:59:46.690
<v Speaker 2>We will fail.

550
00:59:47.330 --> 00:59:50.370
<v Speaker 2>You know, every time you strike an idol and it doesn't break, that's a failure.

551
00:59:51.730 --> 00:59:56.530
<v Speaker 2>Every time you try to leave a habit and you fail, that is just one strike.

552
00:59:56.610 --> 00:59:58.770
<v Speaker 2>Try again, try again, try again.

553
00:59:58.930 --> 01:00:00.050
<v Speaker 2>Our problem is...

554
01:00:00.330 --> 01:00:01.730
<v Speaker 2>and this applies to me.

555
01:00:02.290 --> 01:00:05.810
<v Speaker 2>I can see me talking to myself right here.

556
01:00:06.290 --> 01:00:10.530
<v Speaker 2>Like I give up, you know, I try, I try and then when I fail, it's like, Oh, you know what?

557
01:00:11.050 --> 01:00:11.930
<v Speaker 2>It's not gonna happen.

558
01:00:11.970 --> 01:00:12.370
<v Speaker 2>Why?

559
01:00:13.970 --> 01:00:14.770
<v Speaker 2>Just keep trying.

560
01:00:15.010 --> 01:00:15.570
<v Speaker 2>So what?

561
01:00:15.570 --> 01:00:16.610
<v Speaker 2>Eventually it'll happen.

562
01:00:18.690 --> 01:00:28.290
<v Speaker 2>So, you know, when people learn about these ideas and, you know, one of the reactions is, you know, oh my God, you know, I cannot do this.

563
01:00:28.290 --> 01:00:28.690
<v Speaker 2>Why not?

564
01:00:29.210 --> 01:00:36.170
<v Speaker 2>You know, and that is the wrong concept because the conquest of Makkah should be in the front of our eyes when we're trying to deal with the situation.

565
01:00:37.250 --> 01:00:40.130
<v Speaker 2>Look at how the Kaaba was not cleansed in one strike.

566
01:00:41.250 --> 01:00:42.370
<v Speaker 2>It took a lot of effort.

567
01:00:45.090 --> 01:00:47.490
<v Speaker 2>So, it's gonna take a lot of effort on our part.

568
01:00:47.650 --> 01:00:55.330
<v Speaker 2>But the thing is, when Allah is at the front and center of all of these efforts, it becomes so easy.

569
01:00:56.530 --> 01:00:57.730
<v Speaker 2>Because there's no grudge.

570
01:00:58.130 --> 01:01:00.770
<v Speaker 2>There's no, Oh my God, why do I have to do this?

571
01:01:00.930 --> 01:01:02.050
<v Speaker 2>You know, this is terrible.

572
01:01:02.290 --> 01:01:06.290
<v Speaker 2>Because the idea is now that I'm doing this to please Allah, I'm doing it happily.

573
01:01:07.330 --> 01:01:09.890
<v Speaker 2>I want to do it and that makes it so much easier.

574
01:01:10.050 --> 01:01:12.850
<v Speaker 2>The more you want, the more power it gives in your strength.

575
01:01:14.930 --> 01:01:15.210
<v Speaker 2>Right?

576
01:01:16.450 --> 01:01:22.770
<v Speaker 2>And the most easiest way of doing this, the first step of doing this is Salat.

577
01:01:25.090 --> 01:01:35.970
<v Speaker 2>Our Salat has the concept of breaking idols within its very nature because look at the times of Salat, the most busiest times that we always have.

578
01:01:36.450 --> 01:01:52.930
<v Speaker 2>you know, waking up from our deep sleep, right smack in the middle of the day when we're busy with work, right at the time when we are leaving for work, came home tired, sunset, you know, that's when we have to do Maghrib and then now we're sleepy and tired after a long day of work.

579
01:01:52.930 --> 01:01:56.930
<v Speaker 2>We've eaten so much that I can barely get off the chair and now I have to do Isha.

580
01:01:58.930 --> 01:02:07.730
<v Speaker 2>So Salat has been placed at this, you know, right at the center of the most uncomfortable times and in order to do Salat every single time you have to break an idol.

581
01:02:10.170 --> 01:02:16.850
<v Speaker 2>Because as soon as it's time for prayer the first thing you will have to do every single time is stop doing whatever you're doing.

582
01:02:18.850 --> 01:02:27.410
<v Speaker 2>So now if I am gluttonous, if I eat a lot, Isha will stop me from eating a lot because I know I have to do Isha.

583
01:02:28.050 --> 01:02:36.610
<v Speaker 2>So I will not let that food make me so heavy and feeling so you know full that I am not able to do my salat.

584
01:02:41.090 --> 01:02:42.810
<v Speaker 2>So this is the beauty of salat.

585
01:02:44.450 --> 01:02:49.210
<v Speaker 2>It forces you to leave whoever you're with and turn your face towards Allah.

586
01:02:51.490 --> 01:02:52.210
<v Speaker 2>Salat

587
01:02:52.770 --> 01:02:56.050
<v Speaker 2>is the very concept of la ilaha illallah in action.

588
01:02:56.210 --> 01:02:58.810
<v Speaker 2>You want to see la ilaha illallah in action in your life?

589
01:02:59.010 --> 01:02:59.410
<v Speaker 2>Salaat.

590
01:03:00.970 --> 01:03:03.330
<v Speaker 2>Because that is exactly what you're doing, breaking idols.

591
01:03:05.090 --> 01:03:07.050
<v Speaker 2>And so this is the journey of la ilaha illallah.

592
01:03:07.090 --> 01:03:11.890
<v Speaker 2>It's a difficult journey and every journey requires provisions, right?

593
01:03:12.450 --> 01:03:13.730
<v Speaker 2>That help you get through the journey.

594
01:03:15.250 --> 01:03:18.130
<v Speaker 2>And the provision for this journey is the knowledge of Allah.

595
01:03:20.250 --> 01:03:21.970
<v Speaker 2>which is what we're doing in these sessions.

596
01:03:22.130 --> 01:03:26.370
<v Speaker 2>The more knowledge we have of Allah, the more we will be amazed by His glory.

597
01:03:27.570 --> 01:03:32.610
<v Speaker 2>The more amazed and astonished we are, the more passionate we will become in our love for Him.

598
01:03:33.650 --> 01:03:37.330
<v Speaker 2>The more passionately we love Him, the more we will be obsessed about Him.

599
01:03:37.970 --> 01:03:42.850
<v Speaker 2>The more we're obsessed about Him, the more we will worship Him and submit to His commands.

600
01:03:43.890 --> 01:03:48.370
<v Speaker 2>The more we worship Him, the more we will turn to Him seeking His refuge.

601
01:03:49.650 --> 01:03:57.410
<v Speaker 2>The more we find ourselves under His powerful shelter, the more we will lean on Him, the more we will put our weight on Him for support.

602
01:03:59.170 --> 01:04:02.770
<v Speaker 2>Because in the final analysis, love engenders love.

603
01:04:04.370 --> 01:04:08.370
<v Speaker 2>The more we realize how much He loves us, the more we will love Him back.

604
01:04:08.690 --> 01:04:12.610
<v Speaker 2>The more we love Him back, the more intense He will get in His blessings and mercy.

605
01:04:15.010 --> 01:04:19.010
<v Speaker 2>Wa ista azana rabbukum la inshakartum la azi danna ko

606
01:04:20.210 --> 01:04:24.050
<v Speaker 2>And your master has said that if you are grateful, I will give you more.

607
01:04:24.050 --> 01:04:25.810
<v Speaker 2>I will increase in my blessings.

608
01:04:29.650 --> 01:04:43.090
<v Speaker 1>Wa hir dawa nami hamdulillahi wa bilalameen wassalatu wassalamu ala rasuli saydna Muhammadan khatimin naveen wassaidul mursaleen, wala khiva wassi alibnabi tahilbwasir malalayimatim zuriatima taibi na tahireen salawatullahi wa salamu ali majmaeen al-fatihah
